## Multiple Regression

Adding more predictors lets the model account for other sources of variation at the same time.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(gtsummary)

model <- lm(blood_pressure ~ age + treatment, data = data)
summary(model)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```

Call:
lm(formula = blood_pressure ~ age + treatment, data = data)

Residuals:
    Min      1Q  Median      3Q     Max 
-27.345 -10.457   0.460   8.412  36.488 

Coefficients:
             Estimate Std. Error t value Pr(>|t|)    
(Intercept) 127.61138    7.40163  17.241   <2e-16 ***
age          -0.08746    0.14445  -0.606    0.546    
treatmentB   -2.94412    2.88373  -1.021    0.310    
---
Signif. codes:  0 '***' 0.001 '**' 0.01 '*' 0.05 '.' 0.1 ' ' 1

Residual standard error: 14.41 on 97 degrees of freedom
Multiple R-squared:  0.01408,	Adjusted R-squared:  -0.006248 
F-statistic: 0.6926 on 2 and 97 DF,  p-value: 0.5027
```


:::

